AmiAtari2600 - Atari 2600 emulator for classic Amigas
======================================================

AmiAtari2600 emulates the Atari 2600 (VCS) on AmigaOS 3.x. The emulator drives
the Amiga's custom chips directly (Copper, bitplanes, Paula, BEAMCON0) and
comes with a MUI launcher: game list with filter, game information, screenshots
and the console switches, saved per game.

Contents
--------
  AmiAtari2600       the launcher (MUI) - double-click its icon
  A26                the emulator, started by the launcher; also usable from
                     the Shell
  roms/              put your ROMs here (.bin, .a26, .rom or .zip)
  ReadMe, LICENSE    this file and the licence

The launcher creates db/ (game database) and snaps/ (screenshots) next to
itself. No ROMs are included.

Requirements
------------
Emulator (A26):
  - full speed needs at least a 68060 at 50 MHz (or e.g. PiStorm/Emu68);
    slower CPUs run with frameskip
  - an ECS Agnus (8372A) to switch between PAL and NTSC while running; with an
    OCS Agnus the emulator stays in the machine's own mode
  - nothing else

Launcher (AmiAtari2600):
  - MUI 3.8 or newer, OS 3.x
  - screenshots need picture.datatype V43 (OS 3.2, 3.5/3.9) and a PNG datatype
  - optional: curl and AmiSSL (both on Aminet). With them "Get database" and
    "Get all screenshots" download the libretro game database and screenshots.
    Without them copy the files yourself: the .dat files of libretro-database
    (metadat/no-intro, publisher, developer, releaseyear, genre for
    "Atari - 2600") into db/ as nointro.dat, publisher.dat, developer.dat,
    releaseyear.dat and genre.dat, and screenshots as snaps/<CRC32>.png
    (8 upper-case hex digits, e.g. snaps/1E86DE5A.png)

Starting A26 from the Shell
---------------------------
  A26 <rom> [PAL|NTSC] [COLORS=PAL|NTSC] [TYPE=F8|F6|...] [SKIP=n] [DELAY=n]
      [PORT1] [PRI=n] [NOSOUND] [KILLOS] [PROFILE] [BENCH=n] [FRAMES=n]

  Region and bank switching are detected automatically. PORT1: the joystick in
  the mouse port controls player 2. KILLOS switches the OS off while playing
  (a little faster; network and timers stop).

Keys
----
  Joystick port 2 / cursor keys + Space/Alt   player 1
  F1 / F2     Game Reset / Game Select (hold)
  F3          colour / black and white
  F4 / F5     left / right difficulty
  F6          region: Auto -> NTSC -> PAL -> Auto
  P           pause
  HELP        hard reset
  ESC         quit

